{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced","id":1311925,"title":"The \"Titanomachy\" Supplement Was Just Announced","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-13T18:23:28-07:00","id":1311925,"title":"The \"Titanomachy\" Supplement Was Just Announced","content":"On today's Monday Meeting notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:37:28-07:00","id":1311929,"title":"","content":"I think it got mentioned in the most recent Kickstarter update. Alas, we don't have a lot to go on beyond the name, so everything is just Pure Speculation.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to predict with the authority vested in me by My Own Ego that this is clearly gonna be a book that takes a look at the various Titans throughout the World, goes into &quot;So what makes a Titan?&quot;, breaks down the differences in outlook towards Titans across the Pantheons, and probably give rules for playing a Titanic Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:41:20-07:00","id":1311933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311929#post1311929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it got mentioned in the most recent Kickstarter update. Alas, we don't have a lot to go on beyond the name, so everything is just Pure Speculation.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to predict with the authority vested in me by My Own Ego that this is clearly gonna be a book that takes a look at the various Titans throughout the World, goes into &amp;quot;So what makes a Titan?&amp;quot;, breaks down the differences in outlook towards Titans across the Pantheons, and probably give rules for playing a Titanic Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they answer if Kronos is an Agricultural Titan or a Titan of the passage of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:49:20-07:00","id":1311937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311933#post1311933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope they answer if Kronos is an Agricultural Titan or a Titan of the passage of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a common mistake. Kronos is in no way related to Chronos, the names just sound the same. It'd be like claiming that your coworkers, Shawn and Sean, are the same person because their names are phonetically the same.<br /> <br /> So, probably Agricultural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:50:47-07:00","id":1311938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311937#post1311937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a common mistake. Kronos is in no way related to Chronos, the names just sound the same. It'd be like claiming that your coworkers, Shawn and Sean, are the same person because their names are phonetically the same.<br /> <br /> So, probably Agricultural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, are you by any chance also Shawn Mendes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:52:20-07:00","id":1311939,"title":"","content":"Titanomachy is most well known from Greek Mythology, but it's actual origins are Hititte Religion (along with the basic idea of a Olympian council).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:53:34-07:00","id":1311941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311939#post1311939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titanomachy is most well known from Greek Mythology, but it's actual origins are Hititte Religion (along with the basic idea of a Olympian council).</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? Never heard of it before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T18:59:12-07:00","id":1311943,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my guess would be a break down on the conflicts each pantheon faces, who the titans in question are, how the fight in general is going, some plothooks scattered here and there, the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:02:30-07:00","id":1311945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311939#post1311939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titanomachy is most well known from Greek Mythology, but it's actual origins are Hititte Religion (along with the basic idea of a Olympian council).</div> </div> </div> </div>In Scion, the Titanomachy is a term the game uses to refer to any Pantheon war against Titan figures. For instance, the Deva and the Teotl are pretty ardently in the camp of &quot;Exterminate the Titans&quot;, while you've got some Pantheons like the Manitou who are &quot;There's not a huge difference between Titan and God, TBH&quot; and the Orisha and Loa who are &quot;Most of what you all call Titans are just being smeared by bad PR&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, the word is Greek in origin, but much like Pantheon it's used as a catch-all term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:19:55-07:00","id":1311950,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on &quot;demonization&quot; of earlier deities to justify the rise later ones?<br /> oy, I admit after reading about the Greek Titans and how little info there is, I an looking forward to anything resembling the titans and such early deities, and where the imagination goes with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:51:54-07:00","id":1311961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311938#post1311938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>, are you by any chance also Shawn Mendes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wasn't Canadian the last time I checked, so probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T19:52:32-07:00","id":1311962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311961#post1311961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wasn't Canadian the last time I checked, so probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Dang it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T18:25:56-08:00","id":1370893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1311950#post1311950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on &quot;demonization&quot; of earlier deities to justify the rise later ones?<br /> oy, I admit after reading about the Greek Titans and how little info there is, I an looking forward to anything resembling the titans and such early deities, and where the imagination goes with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am currently reading &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#21282D\"><span style=\"font-family:Poynter\">The Jotunbok: Working With The Giants Of The Northern Tradition&quot; by Raven Kaldera during my lunch break at work. The book postulates that the Jotuns were the gods of the pre-indo-europeans of northern Europe. It further postulates that the gods, the jotuns and the elves can overshadow humans during sex and leave there mark on the resulting offspring. </span></span></div></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:05:27-08:00","id":1370906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370893#post1370893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am currently reading &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#21282D\"><span style=\"font-family:Poynter\">The Jotunbok: Working With The Giants Of The Northern Tradition&quot; by Raven Kaldera during my lunch break at work. The book postulates that the Jotuns were the gods of the pre-indo-europeans of northern Europe. It further postulates that the gods, the jotuns and the elves can overshadow humans during sex and leave there mark on the resulting offspring. </span></span></div></span></div> </div> </div> </div>just as a comment, Jotunblut was a nice PSP, that was basically what you are saying, leaving the mark of your blood in the offspring (it was about serving your blood, but...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:17:57-08:00","id":1370909,"title":"","content":"This is easily the book I'm most excited about that won't specifically add a new pantheon. I was a little confused and disappointed but the ultra-brief mentions most Titans received in the core book, and by the rather minuscule selection of them for each pantheon. (Fenris and Jormungandr weren't even listed). That said, this book rectifies that, so no harm, no foul. So I'm very excited for it, and I hope we get info on a ton of Titans, the number varying, obviously, based on the number that exists for each pantheon. It's going to be essential, in other words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T19:32:18-08:00","id":1370912,"title":"","content":"Pantheons I'm predicting will have loads of Titans (Note that in all of these the Titans have at least one organized cosmological faction within them):<br /> Theoi<br /> Aesir<br /> Deva<br /> Tuatha de Danann<br /> Yazata<br /> <br /> Pantheons I'm predicting will have an average number of Titans:<br /> Teotl<br /> Kami (Could easily go in the first category depending on how obscure you want to go and how powerful you need an entity to be to count as a Titan).<br /> Shen<br /> <br /> Pantheons I'm predicting will have a couple of Titans:<br /> Netjer<br /> Manitou<br /> Nementodevos<br /> <br /> Pantheons I'm predicting (or know) will have no Titans:<br /> Orisha<br /> Loa","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 02-27-2020, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:03:19-08:00","id":1370921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370906#post1370906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> just as a comment, Jotunblut was a nice PSP, that was basically what you are saying, leaving the mark of your blood in the offspring (it was about serving your blood, but...)</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e? Jotunblut was the worst PSP. Hands-down. From every metric.<br /> <br /> It was pretty bad thematically for not really being a Thing that showed up in most Nordic Myth, at least not from the Aesir, AFAIK.<br /> <br /> Mechanically it was the worst PSP in an edition with MANY useless PSPs. Because what did it do? Give your Followers dots of Strength and Stamina.<br /> <br /> Your FOLLOWERS. You know, those barely functional lackeys that will fold like a wet paper bag even WITH the small increase to Strength or Stamina. What's that? At Demigod Tier they may pick up like... 3 dots of E. Strength or Stamina?<br /> <br /> When your opponents are probably packing 4+ dots of Epic Dex? And your Followers have NO dots of Epic Dex?<br /> <br /> Wasted XP, all around. If I had someone ask advice for a 1e game, I'd tell them (amongst other bits of advice) to refund any and all Jotunblut Boon purchases.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for Titanomachy... I figure that they won't give full proportionate weight related to how many enemies each Pantheon has for the total number of Titans per Pantheon, but some Pantheons will have a large number to draw from.<br /> <br /> And I figure the Teotl will have an impressive roster, what with their nightly war against the Star Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-27-2020, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:18:46-08:00","id":1370924,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, I'm most intrigued to see what gets selected for the Kami Titans. Having studied Yokai a lot, there's a ton of potential for them to easily have both the largest and the most eclectic set of Titans. There are strange and monstrous beings that fall under the umbrella of Kami themselves but could be considered Titanic. There are all the many warlords and powerful, specific members that exist amongst the classic Yokai races. And of course, there's all the giant monsters. &quot;Daikaiju&quot; may be a modern term, but it is not a modern concept in Japanese culture. There's so much potential for both weirdness and coolness and I hope they don't just choose the well-known, obvious, choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T20:53:54-08:00","id":1370931,"title":"","content":"I think the Hero book mentions Fujin, Raijin, and Nezumo in particular as Kami Titans.<br /> <br /> And keep in mind, that there's a difference between Titans and Titanspawn. The Various Nasties of Japan are probably Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, dang, I can't remember if I heard any intel whether Izanami is a Primordial or a Titan, nor whether she'd be in the Titanomachy or in the Demigod book. PART of me wants to run her as a Death-focused Titan, but one who's not a very major threat as she's stuck in Yomi. The Underworld that nobody even goes to anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-28-2020, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T22:04:48-08:00","id":1370939,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d throw in Amanozako/Amanosagume as a Passion Titan, and the Amanojaku as her Titanspawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T00:19:40-08:00","id":1370942,"title":"","content":"What is the formal difference between a Titan and a Titanspawn? Is it just degree of power and/or &quot;uniqueness?&quot; Because, if we're just talking power, most of the super-mega-ultra Oni/Kitsune/Tengu etc. are probably at least on the level of Raijin and Fujin. I'm not honestly certain how that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T01:22:05-08:00","id":1370948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370921#post1370921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e? Jotunblut was the worst PSP. Hands-down. From every metric.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, out of theme and deeply low powered, but interesting somehow. Vampiresque... And totally off topic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T02:18:29-08:00","id":1370960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370942#post1370942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the formal difference between a Titan and a Titanspawn? Is it just degree of power and/or &quot;uniqueness?&quot; Because, if we're just talking power, most of the super-mega-ultra Oni/Kitsune/Tengu etc. are probably at least on the level of Raijin and Fujin. I'm not honestly certain how that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Titans are godlike beings consumed by their Purviews.<br /> <br /> Titanspawn is a catch-all term, I believe, for General Spooky Critters of a variety of origins but are usually antagonistic in some way, I believe.<br /> <br /> Most Jotnar are considered Titanspawn. Most Oni would be as well. Hell, some Jotun are probably Titans (Possibly Utgard Loki and definitely Surtr)<br /> <br /> I admit I'm not an expert on all the Oni of Shinto legend, so I dunno if any of them may hypothetically be a Titan. For all I know there may well be a massive Oni whose might and fury was great enough to menace Heaven itself, and all the Amatsukami had to unite in order to cast him down.<br /> <br /> Also, important note: Despite being called Titanspawn, there's no requirement that they be loyal to Titans, AFAIK.<br /> <br /> Edit: So, on a lark, I hit up a friend who's far more knowledgeable about Shintoism than I, and he said that most of the oni he knows about are mostly Hero to Demigod tier. Scary, yes, strong, yes, but usually slain by figures that themselves weren't necessarily Godly. He did, however, also give me the names of a few potential Kami-adjacent Titan figures! <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Kagu-Tsuchi, one of the children of Izanami and Izanagi. His associated Purview is Fire, and he was believed to represent the destructive aspects of it. After he was born, Izanagi beheaded him and cut him into pieces, and the pieces and spilled blood gave birth to eight lesser Godly Beings.</li> <li>Nigihayahi, a divine figure who sired a royal line that served as a competitor to the Imperial Line favored by Amaterasu. Probably associated with the Order Purview.</li> <li>Ibuki Daimyojin, the God of Mount Ibuki. Various legends claim he is either Yamato-no-Orochi or a reincarnation thereof, the beast slain by Susano'o, <i>and</i> the ancestor of the great <i>oni</i> Shuten-Doji. He also has the power to draw forth toxic vapors from the depths of the earth (which slew the hero Yamato Takeru), and this along with his Mountain associations makes him feel like an Earth Titan.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-28-2020, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:01:27-08:00","id":1370973,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m totally looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Izanami is a Primordial, but I can\u2019t remember where I read that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T04:09:20-08:00","id":1370975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370973#post1370973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m totally looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Izanami is a Primordial, but I can\u2019t remember where I read that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think the Kami write up implies that Izanagi and Izanami are Primordials","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T05:26:38-08:00","id":1370987,"title":"","content":"Aside from minor blurbs in the books, does anyone have concrete knowledge on the difference between a Titan and a Primordial? Is it power level? Allegiance? Is it a mechanical difference or is it just story? Inquiring minds (well, maybe just mine) want to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25383-mezryan","name":"Mezryan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T11:30:29-08:00","id":1371056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mezryan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1370987#post1370987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from minor blurbs in the books, does anyone have concrete knowledge on the difference between a Titan and a Primordial? Is it power level? Allegiance? Is it a mechanical difference or is it just story? Inquiring minds (well, maybe just mine) want to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primordials are big. It's usually the classification for the progenitor figures that religions say are the ones that first came when there was nothing.<br /> <br /> There are some figures in the Hero book that are classified as Gods that I would classify as Primordials, tbh. Like Ra/Re. Also, Vishnu and Shiva, as the Deva section has Brahma as a Primordial, and a big part of many Hindu sects is that Brahma is Vishnu is Shiva.<br /> <br /> Titans are godlike beings more focused on their Purview than Gods. A Titan isn't necessarily stronger than a God. And in some cases a divide between God and Titan is a political one.<br /> <br /> Primordials are vast beings, often aloof and detached from the World, and rarely fully manifesting there in their full splendor.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there's a mechanical difference between Gods and Primordials yet, as most od the rules we have are for making a Scion, and thus it's a matter of patronage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T17:13:13-08:00","id":1371117,"title":"","content":"My view of the difference between them is how close to what they represent they are.<br /> <br /> A primordial IS what it represents, Gaia is the planet, Uranus is the sky, Erebus is the daekness, they are primordials.<br /> A titan is moved by what they represent, but are not it, Helio is the titan of the sun, he does all things sun related, but he is not the sun itself, he is a Titan.<br /> A god is responsible for what they represent, but they don\u2019t work as what they represent, Apollo is the god of the sun, but it is not what define his qualities, he is an archer, a musician and a healer too.<br /> <br /> but it\u2019s just my impression of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T04:54:08-08:00","id":1371224,"title":"","content":"The challenge with this is individual Pantheons don't work great with that paradigm. It works pretty solidly with the Theoi, but for instance it breaks down with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann.<br /> <br /> Just going from Hero, we can look at their lineup and see where this more Theoi-centric take on Primordial-Titan-God breaks down.<br /> <br /> Danu isn't anything, she is just an ancestral figure to the Pantheon. She isn't what she represents because she doesn't represent anything, she is just an old, probably dead or otherwise permanently 'off screen' figure whose entire claim to fame is that she is the shared ancestor of the multiple tribes that make up the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Titans are harder to do for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 as I disagree with all of their assigned Purviews, but for instance, Balor. Balor is a Chaos Titan, but, is he motivated by Chaos? No, he is a king in his own right, he is a source of stability and power and wealth for his people, he is just one of multiple Fomori kings who attempts to dominate Ireland. His Purview is the result of his actions, rather than the motivation for his actions. (As a note, I would make Balor probably a War or Epic Strength Titan. In these cases, he still isn't being governed by the Purviews, they're just representations of what he does. Conquest or Might, as the 'evil' eye can also be translated as Piercing Eye)<br /> <br /> For Gods, the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 aren't responsible for anything, they don't represent anything, they're just people who stand around and have supernatural heights of talent and learning in specific professions. D\u00edan C\u00e9cht doesn't represent physicians and isn't responsible for them short of his name showing up in one medical prayer (but so does Goibniu so it doesn't seem to be based on D\u00edan C\u00e9cht being a physician) in the St. Gall gospels. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, what is a Primordial, Titan, and God is loosely defined and varies Pantheon to Pantheon, as if everyone had to use the Theoi model, not a single being in the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann wouldn't qualify for any of the Primordial-Titan-God ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T05:16:27-08:00","id":1371957,"title":"","content":"But the entire idea of Gods, Titans and Primordials is basically Theoi-centric. The word Titan it self is Greek by definition, as well as pan-theon, but for that end pantheon is more general in the meaning.<br /> <br /> Even the definition of a God is very... elusive, as the Orixa/Loa are not gods in their own myths. TDD and Aesirs are gods by power not for being the representation of anything, while the Kami are much more related to their representations, as they are almost literally the spirits of the things they represent.<br /> <br /> You can call Jotuns Titans, but they are not, they are Jotun, and the closest word we have for Jotun in English is Giant (that comes from Gigantes, that we\u2019re not gods neither Titans in Theoi myths, even being sons of Gaia too).<br /> <br /> the Theoi are the center of the entire Scion, not because they are more important, but because they are the standard that was established in 1e and (want it or not) is stil being used on 2e (mainly because of the Titans and Titanomachy)<br /> <br /> TL/DR: We are trying to classify as Apples or Oranges the content of a bag full of all kinds of fruits...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-29-2020, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T05:47:19-08:00","id":1371961,"title":"","content":"I think we can pretty successfully divide the Scion concept of God-Titan-Primordial away from the Theoi-centric perspective with great ease though. I would suggest that the books have already been doing this, such as with the development of the political division of Titans and Gods.<br /> <br /> While Titan-Theoi-Protogenoi is a very Theoi centered conception of things, I think it as a paradigm it is useful beyond just the Theoi. Rather than forcing other Pantheons to follow the Theoi image of things, we can just shrug and go, 'Okay here is the loose concept of these three classes of beings, each Pantheon sets their own internal standards for what qualifies for each of these things' more or less. Danu, Bolg, Fintan, Fomor, and the other progenitor-ancestors make great T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Primordials for instance, all that we need to do to accept them as Primordials is accept that they don't need to follow a Theoi-centric system, even if the system was originally based on the Theoi.<br /> <br /> I think one of the great things about Scion is its willingness to accept the complex and not make concessions where one Pantheon dominates the rest. While it is more wishy washy and unclear on a wide scale, it makes the individual Pantheons work quite well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:32:42-08:00","id":1372002,"title":"","content":"&quot;Look we're calling them Titans for the sake of terminology even if it's not universally applicable, much in the same way we're using Pantheon, a distinctively Greek word, to refer to groups of Gods (and sometimes not-Gods, like the Tuatha) united by a shared cosmology. And sometimes there's some wiggle room.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T14:35:02-08:00","id":1372036,"title":"","content":"I just wish we had different words for metaphysical titans and political titans. Obviously many beings would be both (Apep, Surtr, Ah Puch, etc) but it\u2019s weird that Helios (metaphysical Titan consumes by the Sun purview, but politically part of the Theoi) and most Fomorians (not metaphysically defines by a Purview, but politically arrayed against the Tuatha) get the same term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T18:22:41-08:00","id":1372070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1372036#post1372036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish we had different words for metaphysical titans and political titans. Obviously many beings would be both (Apep, Surtr, Ah Puch, etc) but it\u2019s weird that Helios (metaphysical Titan consumes by the Sun purview, but politically part of the Theoi) and most Fomorians (not metaphysically defines by a Purview, but politically arrayed against the Tuatha) get the same term.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a point that really bothers me. Actually, to properly play the game you have to ignore the original Meaning of Titan and work strictly on the political meaning.<br /> <br /> Same for Primordial, Primordial is a guy that was born from nothing, but not all the progenitors are essentially primordials just because he/she is the first of the pantheon/myth. It seams TDD primordial is not exactally a primordial, just a progenitor, while Ymir is the only primordial for the Aesir, even not being related to them directly. Yet, we probably must consider Primordial = progenitor to better understand the meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T18:15:49-08:00","id":1372208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1372070#post1372070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ymir is the only primordial for the Aesir, .</div> </div> </div> </div>Before Ymir emerged from the ice there was Surt with his sword in Muspelheim. Buri also emerged from the ice, licked free by Audhumla. The unanswered question is where did Audhumla come from and where did she go?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T19:12:47-08:00","id":1372214,"title":"","content":"On a note not found elsewhere in the thread, I vaguely recall there used to be talk about a 'Titanborn' calling so you could play Scions of Titans.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether that early idea carried on, i would like to see mechanical support for playing the children of Titans, even if means being more 'monstrous'. In fact, that makes it more appealing to be honest.<br /> <br /> Given the title of the book, we might see some of that here. Even though the rules for Titans will have to wait until Scion: God 2e is out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T20:50:38-08:00","id":1372219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1311925-the-titanomachy-supplement-was-just-announced?p=1372214#post1372214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a note not found elsewhere in the thread, I vaguely recall there used to be talk about a 'Titanborn' calling so you could play Scions of Titans.<br /> <br /> Regardless of whether that early idea carried on, i would like to see mechanical support for playing the children of Titans, even if means being more 'monstrous'. In fact, that makes it more appealing to be honest.<br /> <br /> Given the title of the book, we might see some of that here. Even though the rules for Titans will have to wait until Scion: God 2e is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on, I have some tidbits from the Scuttlebutt... Titan(ic) Callings!<ul><li>Adversary</li> <li>Destroyer</li> <li>Monster</li> <li>Primeval</li> <li>Tyrant</li> </ul><br /> Now, I say Titan<i>ic</i> because last I heard, quite a few of these Callings can be applied to some Gods in the Hero book (Shiva with Destroyer, for instance), and some Gods in the Demigod book will have some of them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, inherit a Calling from your Patron, inherit their Purview, maybe something with the Virtues, bing bang boom Titan Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 